{
  "description": "Roads and zoning on seed 2026. p1 builds a street and both players zone a strip each side of it. p2 lays a street grid, and both zone over it while its cells are still settling: the strokes wait for the cells to settle (M2 review, #147). A street cut through the first strip by p1 on tick 6 goes on, since a road command never waits behind a stroke, and its walk keeps the strokes waiting; p2's stroke over it, sent on tick 6, waits behind p2's first. The cells settle by tick 14, so the strokes are still waiting when p1 pauses on tick 9; while paused the walk finishes and they apply at once, p1's and both of p2's, with a stroke of two crossed rectangles. A clear and a rectangle at the size cap, sent on tick 12, wait for tick 14, where one stroke a tick applies (`cellCommandsPerTick`): the clear on tick 14 and the rectangle on tick 15. A bulldoze of a zoned piece of the first street on tick 14. Recorded again in #358, when the settle's slices were measured again and grew to more ticks.",
